{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/575962-first-change-of-the-changing-breeds","id":575962,"title":"First Change of the Changing Breeds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-01T20:08:35-07:00","id":575962,"title":"First Change of the Changing Breeds","content":"When the changing breeds go through their first, well, <i>change,</i> do they all fall into a rage, like the garou? Or do they have different ways of going about it? I glanced through the CB core, but failed to find anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T20:57:06-07:00","id":575994,"title":"","content":"A lot of them do, a few don't. Ananasi find their emotions getting muted and distant instead, while Mokole dream up a shape without much in the way of raging. Nuwisha firsts, at least as presented for the Rage character in Warriors of the Apocalypse, tend to be bizarre affairs where weird shit happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T01:28:58-07:00","id":576214,"title":"","content":"One Corax First Change ends up with the Homid in Corvid form perched on the roof of a very tall building with no idea how he got there, less idea how to get down and another &quot;raven&quot; perched some distance away wildly cackling at his bewildered expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T08:05:03-07:00","id":607899,"title":"","content":"Gurahl receive dreams and visions from whatever mentor finds them. Their dreams guide them to travel whatever absurd distance they have to take to find their mentor, who might not even be the nearest Gurahl. After probably crossing half a continent to find another of their kind, they have learned something about surviving in the wild and possibly already changed forms.<br /> <br /> But I can't recall offhand whether they have the rage-filled change before that. I think maybe they do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rokea just sort of start feeling enlightened as they go from shark to Sapient Magical Shark and suddenly understand things around them in a new way. Then they feel compelled to visit the nearest underwater caern, where they receive a personal vision from Sea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ratkin get bitten by another Ratkin, which gives them a horrible spiritual disease. If they survive, they experience trippy nightmares that start eroding their sanity, and then a Ratkin watches over them until they're healed and tells them what's up. Crazy shit happens and one way or another, the only way to make sense of their life is to join the crazy full-tilt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My impression of Bastet and Ajaba is that they go through much the same kind of violent, Rage-fuelled First Change as Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nagah start [redacted].<br /> Oh god no wait donaaarrrghghllglblll<br /> *dies*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 07-30-2015, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T12:46:40-07:00","id":608351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/575962-first-change-of-the-changing-breeds?p=607899#post607899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gurahl receive dreams and visions from whatever mentor finds them...<br /> But I can't recall offhand whether they have the rage-filled change before that. I think maybe they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some do and some don't. The breed-book sort of implies that it depends upon the situation. In one instance, an ursine wearbear winds up slaughtering a group of hunters in a frenzy. In another, the character (a homid) is walking through a parking lot when a guy changing a flat tire is trapped underneath a truck when it slips off the jack. Dude freaks out, goes into their equivalent to Crinos, picks up the truck and flings it aside like a toy -- to rescue the guy.<br /> <br /> It is basically implied that while Gurahl have Rage and can frenzy as Garou do, since their Rage works differently, the frenzied First-Change of the werewolves is significantly less common.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T14:52:26-07:00","id":608456,"title":"","content":"Tough characterized by cold thinking, the first change of an Ananasi is usualy dominated by hunger, so it tends to be indeed very similar to a Frenzy. But the werespider is likely to remember everything and not be all that sad about wat they had done.<br /> <br /> But there are exceptions, since their feelings aren't usualy so completely muted, and some aren't muted at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:10:01-07:00","id":609815,"title":"","content":"So, would we do a list?<br /> <br /> Garou: frenzy<br /> Ananasi: Hunger and feeding<br /> Mokol\u00e9: Slumber and dreaming (how much time?)<br /> Corax: weird crow experience.<br /> <br /> Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:16:43-07:00","id":609819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/575962-first-change-of-the-changing-breeds?p=609815#post609815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mokol\u00e9: Slumber and dreaming (how much time?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no guideline given to determine how long, but it doesn't seem to take more time than it would for someone to nod off and have a dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:26:50-07:00","id":609826,"title":"","content":"This is all from memory or my interpretation, so I could be wrong:<br /> I always pictured Nuwisha going into hysterical laughing fits. Kinda like a humor Frenzy. The Nuwisha book was pathetically small and doesn't go into detail on lots of thing related to Nuwisha life, so you just kinda of have to make it up as you go.<br /> <br /> The Gurahl book story fluff has the character possibly learning to shapeshift through his dreams. As others have stated, changing early to protect or help someone is also likely.<br /> <br /> For the Mokole, I like that idea of a long, deep slumber. Maybe for a few days even. But yea, they never actually specify.<br /> <br /> Rokea gain heightened sentience and feel the pull of Sea to a nearby Grotto where they will either get direction from Sea itself, or meet another Rokea along the way who will teach them.<br /> <br /> Ratkin suffer the Birthing Plague. Some die horribly, some get better, and the rest become Ratkin. While in fever fits, even before changing, they can suffer Frenzy or Rapture. Newer information seems to indicate that the Birthing Plague could take weeks to months (possibly years) to pass. At least that interpretation would stop hundreds of thousands of Ratkin from bubbling up from under NYC come the Apocalypse (2 rats for every person, 12 million people, 10% chance of becoming Ratkin).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 07-31-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}